# Build context for the leerie image.
#
# The Dockerfile bakes orchestrator/, scripts/, prompts/, and .claude-plugin/
# into the image so Fly.io Machines can run without a bind mount (§0.5).
# Exclude everything else to keep the build context lean — .git, tests,
# caches, and docs are not needed inside the image and traversing them over
# the host-to-VM bridge (on Colima/macOS) wastes time.
#
# LOCAL MODE: the orchestrator source is bind-mounted at runtime
#   (-v $LEERIE_HOME:/work/.leerie-image:ro), so build-context contents are
#   irrelevant — the COPY instructions below are shadowed by the mount.
#
# REGISTRY / FLY MODE: there is no bind-mount, so the COPY instructions
#   in the Dockerfile bake orchestrator/, scripts/, and prompts/ into
#   /work/.leerie-image/ inside the image. The build context must include
#   those paths and exclude host-only / run-state artifacts.
#
# We negate Dockerfile + .dockerignore so legacy builders (older docker
# build / some podman modes) that honor `*` literally still find them.
# Modern BuildKit always reads them regardless.

# Default: exclude everything, then selectively allow.
*

# Build definition files — always needed.
!Dockerfile
!.dockerignore

# Python runtime deps — installed inside the image (see Dockerfile
# `pip3 install -r /tmp/requirements.txt`).
!requirements.txt

# Orchestrator source — baked into /work/.leerie-image/orchestrator/.
!orchestrator/
!orchestrator/leerie.py

# Chain subsystem — baked into /app/chain/ in the coordinator image
# (see chain/Dockerfile). Not used by the worker image. Both this
# directory entry and chain/Dockerfile itself must be allow-listed:
# the coordinator build context is the repo root (per chain/Dockerfile
# docstring) and the dockerignore default `*` would otherwise exclude
# everything.
!chain/
!chain/Dockerfile

# Shell scripts — baked into /work/.leerie-image/scripts/.
!scripts/
!scripts/container-entry.sh
!scripts/new-worktree.sh
!scripts/setup-run.sh
!scripts/integrate.sh
!scripts/finalize.sh
!scripts/cleanup.sh
!scripts/install.sh
!scripts/runtime-install.sh
# Chain-mode worker scripts — exit hook is sourced by
# scripts/remote/provision.sh's decide_teardown trap; heartbeat is
# background-started by scripts/container-entry.sh when LEERIE_CHAIN_ID
# is set. The recursive `!scripts/` line above already includes them;
# the individual entries here match the convention so the manifest
# stays in sync with /opt/leerie-image/scripts/ contents.
!scripts/leerie-chain-exit-hook.sh
!scripts/leerie-chain-heartbeat.sh
# Smoke scripts — not baked into the image (not under /opt/leerie-image/
# at runtime), but kept in the build context so a future change that
# does include them doesn't silently miss the files.
!scripts/smoke/
!scripts/smoke/chain-trivial.sh
!scripts/smoke/chain-failure-modes.sh

# Worker prompts — baked into /work/.leerie-image/prompts/.
!prompts/
!prompts/classifier.md
!prompts/planner.md
!prompts/implementer.md
!prompts/conformer.md
!prompts/integrator.md
!prompts/reconciler.md
!prompts/provision.md
!prompts/judge.md
!prompts/patch_generator.md
!prompts/_clarification_filter.md

# Plugin manifest — baked into /work/.leerie-image/.claude-plugin/.
!.claude-plugin/
